republic-function.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P5 (S16): "lives well" is taken as faring well, prospering, so that one is blessed and happy in P5 and as living out the soul's function (life) excellently, as a well-working soul does where lives_well is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C2 (S18) does not follow (republic-function.logic.r2.sense1)
republic-function.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C2 (S18): D = {another}; happy = ∅, just = {another}, lives_well = {another}, lives_well_2 = ∅
